    "feedSummary": "Rosemary Lahasky, Director of Workforce and Infrastructure Initiatives at Meta, joins Kevin Frazier, Director of the AI Innovation and Law Program at the University of Texas School of Law and a Senior Editor at Lawfare, from Meta's DC studio to discuss America's Workforce Academy. This seemingly \"too good to be true\" program is not the stuff of make believe. Meta is paying people to receive training in in-demand fields and guaranteeing them a job upon the completion of a four-week curriculum. It's a marked improvement upon other approaches, which are often characterized by low completion rates and poor job placement. Perhaps most importantly, it's already channeling people into new jobs across the country.",
    "doomIndexInputSummary": "Scaling Laws: Meta's Big Investment in Workforce Training with Rosemary Lahasky. Rosemary Lahasky, Director of Workforce and Infrastructure Initiatives at Meta, joins Kevin Frazier, Director of the AI Innovation and Law Program at the University of Texas School of Law and a Senior Editor at Lawfare, from Meta's DC studio to discuss America's Workforce Academy. This seemingly \"too good to be true\" program is not the stuff of make believe. Meta is paying people to receive training in in-demand fields and guaranteeing them a job upon the completion of a four-week curriculum. It's a marked improvement upon other approaches, which are often characterized by low completion rates and poor job placement. Perhaps most importantly, it's already channeling people into new jobs across the country."
